f 1079 #uuid "9e6aa259-14bb-55a0-a32b-6f1dd8102da1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547929 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547929 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547929 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547929 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186547616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547929 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b50ec26a-cc99-5796-8813-5d5595ca224f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547939 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186547785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547939 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547939 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547939 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186547554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547939 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c0937dc5-3ee6-51bf-8cbf-009d6a1d471d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547983 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547983 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547983 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340803" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547983 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547983 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{3}$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547983 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c3a98af-770d-5596-b478-235b18fb3ea6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547983 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{3} \\\\  & =-{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547992 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547992 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547992 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547992 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic extensions of some functions from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the constant Fourier coefficient of $-5f(x)-2g(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547992 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c275290-69db-55d0-83e9-26518022c1c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186547992 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $-5f(x)-2g(x)$ are\n\n- $-5{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $-5{a}_{n}-2{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-5{b}_{n}-2{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the constant Fourier coefficient of $-5f(x)-2g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-5{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548050 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548050 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548050 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548050 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic extensions of some functions from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $6\\text{th}$ Fourier sine coefficient of $-3f(x)-2g(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548050 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c68b418a-a9c2-512b-93fe-1e0b537572e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548050 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $-3f(x)-2g(x)$ are\n\n- $-3{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $-3{a}_{n}-2{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-3{b}_{n}-2{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $6$th sine coefficient of $-3f(x)-2g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-3{b}_{6}-2{d}_{6}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548078 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186547939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548078 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340781" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548078 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548078 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of a function from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $7$th sine Fourier coefficient of $f(-x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548078 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f98d94e0-3737-5c43-aa65-d5af57241d7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548078 #edb/ref 1074 "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nRecall that the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(-x)$ are\n\n- ${a}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ${a}_{n}$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-{b}_{n}$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $7$th sine coefficient of $f(-x)$ is $-{b}_{7}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
